<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <!-- net8.0-windows with UseWPF rather than plain net8.0, because McpBridgeAddOn.cs
         uses real WPF types (System.Windows.Window, Application.Current, Dispatcher,
         VisualTreeHelper). On Windows those resolve for real and need no stubbing.
         What still blocks compiling the bridge itself is NinjaTrader's own type
         surface; tests/README.md records the exact measurement and the remedy. -->
    <TargetFramework>net8.0-windows</TargetFramework>
    <UseWPF>true</UseWPF>
    <DefineConstants>TESTING</DefineConstants>
    <!-- The harness plus every bridge source that names no NinjaTrader type. When the
         bridge itself becomes compilable (tests/README.md), add addons/McpBridgeAddOn.cs
         and the vendored core here. -->
    <EnableDefaultCompileItems>false</EnableDefaultCompileItems>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="BridgeSourceTests.cs" />
    <!--
      P3-111. This WAS a hand-typed list of eight addon files, each with its own comment.
      It is now a glob with one exclusion, for the reason `tools/check_bridge_parses.py`
      stopped being a hand-typed list of two in the same session: a maintained inventory of
      "the files we look at" drifts silently the moment someone adds a ninth, and the symptom
      is a green run that inspected less than it claimed. Adding BridgeBarsQuery.cs and
      BridgeQueryValue.cs by hand here would have been the third instance in one day.

      The glob is the P2-27 rule stated mechanically: EVERY addon source that names no
      NinjaTrader type is EXECUTED by this project, automatically, from the moment it exists.
      McpBridgeAddOn.cs is the one exclusion, because NinjaTrader's type surface is what
      still blocks compiling it (tests/README.md records the measurement and the remedy);
      when that changes, delete the Exclude rather than adding an Include.

      ⚠️ If a newly added addon file DOES name an NT8 type, this build breaks. That is the
      intended failure and it is the loud one: the alternative is the file quietly sitting
      outside every test the repo has, which is the condition P2-27 exists to end.

      Why each file is here is recorded in its own header, which is where it stays true.
    -->
    <!-- IndicatorTestAddOn.cs is excluded for the SAME reason as McpBridgeAddOn.cs: it derives
         from AddOnBase and uses NinjaTrader.Cbi/Data/Gui/Core, none of which the harness stubs.
         Added 2026-08-18 by bfb1c99/60bca1c, which the glob then pulled into the test build and
         broke it with 10 CS0234/CS0246 errors. ⚠️ Neither commit had reached CI, so nothing had
         reported the break, and a no-build run of the stale binary still printed a
         clean pass, which is exactly what a working suite looks like. -->
    <Compile Include="../addons/*.cs" Exclude="../addons/McpBridgeAddOn.cs;../addons/IndicatorTestAddOn.cs" />
    <PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json" Version="13.0.3" />
    <!-- cp1252 is native on net48 (NT8) but NOT on net8.0-windows. F-17's mojibake repair
         reads the code page, so the harness that exercises BridgeConnectionPlan must be
         able to. Registered in Run() via CodePagesEncodingProvider.Instance. -->
    <PackageReference Include="System.Text.Encoding.CodePages" Version="8.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
